      "error_message": "AccessKeyControllerTest/AuthControllerTest: all requests return 200 with empty body, isForbidden() assertions fail with 'Status expected:<403> but was:<200>'",
      "file": "backend/src/test/java/at/querchecker/auth/AccessKeyControllerTest.java",
      "root_cause": "@MockBean SessionCookieAuthFilter (a concrete OncePerRequestFilter wired into the Spring Security chain via SecurityConfig.addFilterBefore) causes Mockito to mock doFilter() itself to a no-op that never calls chain.doFilter() — every request is silently swallowed by the mocked filter, so the controller is never invoked and MockMvc sees a default empty 200 response. Separately, LocalProfileAuthFilter (@Profile(\"!prod\")) is also auto-included by @WebMvcTest since no profile is active by default in tests, so it auto-grants SUPERUSER to every request, defeating the withoutSuperuserRole_isForbidden tests too.",
      "fix": "Never @MockBean a Filter bean that's part of the security chain. Instead mock its real constructor dependencies (UserSessionRepository, AccessKeyRepository) so the real filter runs, and add @ActiveProfiles(\"prod\") to the @WebMvcTest so LocalProfileAuthFilter (@Profile(\"!prod\")) is excluded, matching real prod auth behavior.",
