      "id": "bug-065",
      "timestamp": "2026-07-07T16:00:53.000Z",
      "error_message": "POST /api/auth/keys/{id}/revoke -> 500 InvalidDataAccessApiUsageException: No EntityManager with actual transaction available for current thread - cannot reliably process 'remove' call",
      "file": "backend/src/main/java/at/querchecker/auth/AccessKeyService.java",
      "root_cause": "AccessKeyService.revoke() called userSessionRepository.deleteByAccessKeyId(id), a Spring Data JPA derived delete query. Unlike save()/findById(), a derived deleteBy... query loads-then-removes each entity via entityManager.remove(), which requires an actual writable transaction bound to the thread -- the repository proxy does not provide one for this call path on its own. Only found by manually exercising the endpoint end-to-end via curl against the running dev backend; the Mockito-based AccessKeyServiceTest mocks the repository entirely, so it never touches a real EntityManager/transaction and couldn't catch this.",
      "fix": "Added @Transactional to AccessKeyService.revoke(), matching the project's existing convention (WhListingService, WhItemService, etc. annotate service methods that perform repository writes/deletes beyond a single save()).",
      "tags": [
        "spring-data-jpa",
        "transactional",
        "java",
        "runtime-verification"
      ],
